    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Quillsen proudly presents this attractive own-door, south facing, studio apartment to the market. Approached via striking granite steps and a private period entrance, No. 5 enjoys a unique sense of privacy and independence rarely associated with apartment living.\n\nOccupying a prime position on prestigious Charleston Road, Sherborne Court is within a leisurely stroll of St. Stephen`s Green and moments from the unrivalled amenities of both Ranelagh and Rathmines.\n\nNo. 5 is bright, deceptively spacious and presented in turnkey condition. Extending to approximately 27 sqm. / 290 sqft., the thoughtfully designed accommodation comprises an entrance lobby, a spacious living area with impressive ceiling height, a large south facing uPVC Georgian-style double glazed window, a solid-fuel open fireplace and a bespoke built-in wall bed and wardrobe unit, maximising both space and functionality.\n\nThere is a kitchenette tucked away off the living area and the bathroom is positioned off the entrance lobby. Further enhancing the appeal of this unique offering are the benefits of an external laundry room and residents` parking.\n\nThe convenience of the location speaks for itself. There is an enviable choice of shopping outlets, restaurants, bars and cafés on offer in both Ranelagh and Rathmines. The Omniplex and Stella cinemas provide excellent entertainment options, while nearby Belgrave Square offers beautiful open green spaces and mature trees. To complete the picture and further underscore the convenience of the location, the Luas at Ranelagh is within a five-minute walk.\n\nOffered with vacant possession, No. 5 represents an excellent opportunity for both owner-occupiers and investors alike.\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Lobby - 1m (3'3\") x 1.7m (5'7\")\nWith built in storage and large semicircular fan light.\n\n\nMain Room - 4.2m (13'9\") x 4.2m (13'9\")\nOpen fire place as a focal point, Georgian style uPVC double glazed window, picture rail, centre rose, hot press, high-quality built in wardrobe and wall bed.\n\nKitchen - 1.9m (6'3\") x 1.9m (6'3\")\nWall and floor units, stainless steel sink, electric oven, hob and extractor fan.\n\n\nBathroom - 1.6m (5'3\") x 1.8m (5'11\")\nWC, whb, bath, mixer shower and extractor fan. \n\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Attractive own door studio apartment on Charleston Road </li><li> Striking granite steps and period entrance </li><li> Bright decptively spacious south facing accommodation </li><li> Beside both Ranelagh and Rathmines. Within 5 minutes walk of the Luas </li><li> Strolling distance to St. Stephen`s Green, Grafton Street and the city centre </li><li> Solid fuel open fireplace. Bespoke built-in wall bed and wardrobe. </li><li> Residents` parking </li><li> Communal laundry room </li><li> Annual service charge: Approx. 1,800</li></ul>"
